  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 230 PM EDT Thursday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Warm weather and chances for showers and storms \nstart today and continue into the weekend.\n\nGOES water vapor channels continue to depict a strong upper \nridge centered over the lower Mississippi Valley, with a \nflattened trough sliding ESE across the Great Lakes. At the \nsurface, high pressure is centered from along the Southeast \ncoast to off the Mid-Atlantic coast, with a cold front well to \nour NW over the Ohio Valley. Mostly sunny and warm with \ntemperatures in the lower to mid 80s. There is a line of \nshowers/tstms that has developed across northern VA in vicinity \nof a lee side trough. This activity is expected to push SE into \nNW portions of the CWA over the next few hours, before rapidly \ndissipating by this evening and struggling to reach a line from \nthe Richmond metro to Salisbury. Otherwise, partly cloudy and \nmild tonight with low temperatures in the upper 60s to lower \n70s.\n\nBy Friday, the cold front passes through the area early in the \nmorning as a high pressure builds south out of the Great Lakes. \nCAMs continue to hint at some post-frontal showers/tstms, mainly\nover the SW half of the area. Will note, QPF with this activity\nis minimal (0.1 to 0.25\" across the far SW). In addition to the\nshowers, with the front moving through the morning temperatures\nmay struggle to warm especially across the north. High \ntemperatures Friday likely range from the low to mid 80s N and \nupper 80s to possible 90F S. Mostly dry and somewhat cooler \n(more seasonal) on Saturday behind the front with highs around \n80F/lower 80s. The front likely lifts back to the N as a warm \nfront Sunday. Still mainly dry Sunday with only low chc PoPs NW.\nWarmer with high temperatures in the lower 80s at the coast to \nthe mid/upper 80s inland.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A gradual pattern change with increased rain \nchances and cooler temperatures evolves during the early to \nmiddle portion of next week.\n\nA gradual pattern change begins to evolve by early next week. \nAnother cold front slowly slides S across the region Monday into\nMonday night. There is a chc of showers/tstms with deeper \nmoisture in place and high temperatures ranging from around 80F \nN to the mid/upper 80s S. A decent synoptic agreement continues \nfrom the ECMWF, CMC, AND GFS ensembles showing a strong upper \nlevel ridge building over Hudson Bay. At the surface, this \nallows for the potential of a strong high pressure to center \nitself over Eastern Canada into northern New England. This \npattern would lead to onshore flow, higher rain chances, and \ncooler temperatures by Tuesday/Wednesday.",
